{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542227-why-patricia-of-bollingbroke-sucks","id":1542227,"title":"Why Patricia of Bollingbroke sucks??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-15T23:33:46-07:00","id":1542227,"title":"Why Patricia of Bollingbroke sucks??","content":"For some reason, one of the - and against my preferred view - if not the first big Anarch, who is built in text as the greatest agitator and rebel of the Anarchs and Brujah, also lacks any weight to her doings and will. Putting it plainly she sucks, and I wished it weren't so. <br /> <br /> Let's start with the fact that she was the wife of a killed peasant who took a famous peasant leader as a lover, all of whom seem to be way more important than herself in her own story. And that trend continue... Robin freaking Hood Embraces her and takes her out of jail. And she takes the name of her late lover, so she buries her own identity even further in lieu of other guys.<br /> <br /> Than she kills the crap baron who made her miserable, which is very cool. But instead of staying in England, and fighting... I don't know... a thousand year old tyrant like Mithras, or Queen Anne, she runs away. And goes to... Spain, where she... basically stumbles on Anarchs... who basically stumble on Hardestadt's castle? which sometimes is in Bavaria and sometimes in Spain? and then a band of untrained, kind of lost fledlings, murder one of the most powerful Ventrue of the current time, in his own castle... Someone Patricia could've never had heard of before. <br /> And ... in the end, Hardestadt is not dead! So she probably looked like a chump?! I don't know. This 'Hardestadt is not dead' spiel always was weird for me, did they call the Anarchs out? What happened? Either way... Anarch War goes, nothing important occurs for Patricia, maybe just some agitating or not<br /> <br /> Then Convention of Thorns! Our Rebel Leader, who is determined to kill Hardestadt now, for some reason. Tries to kill him, and fails because guns are nothing to vampires.... she didn't tried before? She think someone with Fortitude wouldn't take those shot? And let me remind you that of all the elders she could attack, like the ones in her homeland, she decided to attack the guy she just kind of stumbled into killing, and &quot;failed&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> And... we skip a lot of time, she changes her name; she runs, Helena comes into contact with Patricia, and bam, methuseleah puppet of Helena forever.... than they go to America (because why would two centuries-old elders go anywhere else) and bicker with Critias, because Helena. And then she starts to like... planes? funny, but I can understand it perfectly, just a bit random. <br /> So she jobs for Helena, then runs again to NY, and starts jobbing for Lambach Ruthven... and that's that... Great leader she is, great symbol; not even a tragic story, it just feels accidentally pathetic I don't know. <br /> <br /> Any information I'm missing that throws new light into her?<br /> Are my views a bit true?<br /> Is there a way to make her stand with dignity alongside Gratiano, Vykos, Dominique de Tourraine, Vasantasena, Lugoj?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T23:38:30-07:00","id":1542228,"title":"","content":"Yeah the big problem with her personality is shes just a rebel for its own sake. She isnt really working towards anything so genrally just seems to be reflexivly pushing back meaning as a character she has the classic anarch issue of only having the aesthetic of dissidence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T23:50:49-07:00","id":1542229,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much &quot;dignity&quot; those other Anarchs have over Tyler. Lugoj actually died, his identity stolen by the ancient he supposedly destroyed. Dominique at this point has very little influence within the sect, her ideals having been defeated in several Sabbat Civil Wars. Gratiano is either a liar or a deluded pawn who does not even know he is a pawn. Only Vykos is possibly an Anarch/Sabbat who triumphed over the long courses of the centuries, and if we don't think he is a Loyalist he is actually someone who betrayed his ideals for power.<br /> <br /> As for Tyler herself, I don't think someone who chooses to remember her lover means she &quot;buries her own identity.&quot; I don't think the character has much to apologize for prior to Helena enslaving her. If she is somehow forgotten among the Sabbat, it says more for the OOC writers of the Sabbat than the NPC members of the Sabbat and the Brujah anti-tribu who should be remembering her as a pillar of the sect.<br /> <br /> Yeah, being enslaved by Helena is a tragedy, but there are lots of tragedies among all vampires of all sects. The Sabbat as a sect is hopelessly compromised according to the original lore, so if you are going to call Tyler out you must call out the entire sect. The only thing that distinguishes Tyler from other &quot;failures&quot; is that instead of being known in the Sabbat, she's known within the Camarilla instead in an alternate identity. Yet when you compare the Camarilla to the Sabbat post-third civil war, which sect is actually more in favor of freedom?<br /> <br /> If you really want to make Tyler a significant figure among the Anarchs and Sabbat, you just need to fill in the relatively sparse history between the diablerie of Hardestadt and the early Camarilla-Sabbat wars. Unfortunately, the writers and developers choose to not consider the Brujah anti-tribu as one of the pillars of the Sabbat. Yet any critical reading of the early sources clearly shows they should be considered one of the pillars of that sect along with the Lasombra and Tzimisce. In my chronicles, I have that be so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T14:48:43-07:00","id":1542273,"title":"","content":"You could also that Tyler is also shows what the Brujah's clan weakness of being rebels for the sake of it and don't have a real goal in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T15:54:15-07:00","id":1542278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542227-why-patricia-of-bollingbroke-sucks?p=1542273#post1542273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also that Tyler is also shows what the Brujah's clan weakness of being rebels for the sake of it and don't have a real goal in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess so<br /> <br /> But that would be just sad );<br /> And that would make the entire Clan Brujah suck instead of being flawed, for me anyhow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T18:42:12-07:00","id":1542282,"title":"","content":"It can still work that the Brujah are agents of change and seek ways to do it and that there flaw that there passion for causes blind them to the reality that there clan all have different views of how to accomplish it and get into each other's ways.<br /> <br /> A good creative talent can make the clan great again as there is enough of a good foundation to work with. The Brujah are not like Ur-Shugi that has nothing to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T04:58:37-07:00","id":1542305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542227-why-patricia-of-bollingbroke-sucks#post1542227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, one of the - and against my preferred view - if not the first big Anarch, who is built in text as the greatest agitator and rebel of the Anarchs and Brujah, also lacks any weight to her doings and will. Putting it plainly she sucks, and I wished it weren't so.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the fact that she was the wife of a killed peasant who took a famous peasant leader as a lover, all of whom seem to be way more important than herself in her own story. And that trend continue... Robin freaking Hood Embraces her and takes her out of jail. And she takes the name of her late lover, so she buries her own identity even further in lieu of other guys.<br /> <br /> Than she kills the crap baron who made her miserable, which is very cool. But instead of staying in England, and fighting... I don't know... a thousand year old tyrant like Mithras, or Queen Anne, she runs away. And goes to... Spain, where she... basically stumbles on Anarchs... who basically stumble on Hardestadt's castle? which sometimes is in Bavaria and sometimes in Spain? and then a band of untrained, kind of lost fledlings, murder one of the most powerful Ventrue of the current time, in his own castle... Someone Patricia could've never had heard of before.<br /> And ... in the end, Hardestadt is not dead! So she probably looked like a chump?! I don't know. This 'Hardestadt is not dead' spiel always was weird for me, did they call the Anarchs out? What happened? Either way... Anarch War goes, nothing important occurs for Patricia, maybe just some agitating or not<br /> <br /> Then Convention of Thorns! Our Rebel Leader, who is determined to kill Hardestadt now, for some reason. Tries to kill him, and fails because guns are nothing to vampires.... she didn't tried before? She think someone with Fortitude wouldn't take those shot? And let me remind you that of all the elders she could attack, like the ones in her homeland, she decided to attack the guy she just kind of stumbled into killing, and &quot;failed&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> And... we skip a lot of time, she changes her name; she runs, Helena comes into contact with Patricia, and bam, methuseleah puppet of Helena forever.... than they go to America (because why would two centuries-old elders go anywhere else) and bicker with Critias, because Helena. And then she starts to like... planes? funny, but I can understand it perfectly, just a bit random.<br /> So she jobs for Helena, then runs again to NY, and starts jobbing for Lambach Ruthven... and that's that... Great leader she is, great symbol; not even a tragic story, it just feels accidentally pathetic I don't know.<br /> <br /> Any information I'm missing that throws new light into her?<br /> Are my views a bit true?<br /> Is there a way to make her stand with dignity alongside Gratiano, Vykos, Dominique de Tourraine, Vasantasena, Lugoj?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the bit about Hardestadt, is that she killed Hardestadt the Elder, the 5th generation vampire, but later when he resurfaces, its Hardestadt the Younger, eg: J\u00fcrgen von Verden the 6th generation vampire. Tyler also didn't just kill Hardestadt the Elder, she diablerized him, going from 8th to 6th generation. She wasn't the one who injured him, though, and she is an opportunist who found an opening to advance herself generationaly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The outcome of the attack on Hardestadt's unlife was kept largely a secret, however. As Hardestadt the Younger rose to leadership pretending to be his sire, the sect propaganda created a tale where she failed at her endeavor. Therefore, Camarilla society at large does not know that <i>Patricia of Bollingbroke</i> diablerized Hardestadt.\u200b&quot; </div> </div> </div>She failed to kill Hardestadt the Younger, who she went after because she's one of the few who knows that he is not really who he says he is. This failure forces her to flee to South America, where she runs into Helena who is hiding here after her battles with Menele. Helena Dominates and Bloodbond's her and sends her to Chicago later.<br /> <br /> Helena's whole thing is following around Menele to try to kill him over their centuries old feud. Helena has methuselah's thirst, and only likes to eat Female Kindred for the most part. You can see this in Chicago Chronicles when she awakens and eats her 5th generation childe. This is one of the reasons Melinda Gabraith got involved with Shaitan and the Sabbat. Tyler is a backup snack when she is no longer useful to Helena. As for going to Lambach, its mostly the same reason. Most likely to hit up the vaulderie to break the bloodbond.<br /> <br /> Helena has been using her as a poster child for the Anarchs to draw in more tasty snacks though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T11:39:36-07:00","id":1542326,"title":"","content":"I don't think Helena and Menele really want to &quot;kill&quot; each other as they are defined by that feud and it's the only thing that has kept them going for all this time and by the recent version of Chicago By Night she is trying to fill that void with her rival's disappearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T12:20:51-07:00","id":1542331,"title":"","content":"To be fair, there's no ability to do a rebellion in England against Mithras.<br /> <br /> <b>WHY THERE ARE NO ANARCHS IN ENGLAND</b><br /> <br /> This actually came up in my FALL OF LONDON campaign where one of the players explained that the Anarchs are a new phenomenon and only came into existence after WW2.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Mithras never had to deal with any internal rebellion. There was no Anarch revolt in England.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Bullshit, every Prince does.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Every Camarilla Prince but Mithras was not a prince. He was a god.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All the more reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;*deliberate sigh* Listen, dipshit, I'm not speaking figuratively. I'm saying that when you met Mithras, you believed he was a god and wanted to worship him. He was the fairest, bestest, most awesome son of a bitch who ever lived. His power over making you love him was beyond question and the only people who could challenge that were other ancients that were just as powerful. Mithras hated the Tremere because the Council of Seven could do that. Maybe the Inner Council. Some Red Listers. Plus, Mithras thought he was a benevolent tyrant and tried to act that way.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Bullshit. No such thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, but the Anarchs are still vampires and they can only propose something similar. Richard II, for example, was the first King of England to ever have his head on a block. That was because Mithras hated him for breaking his word to the rebels. Hence why Henry the Fourth came to power a few decades later.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's a fucking fairy tale if I ever heard it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And yet it's the story people believed. Because Mithras wanted them to. So they did.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T12:34:44-07:00","id":1542332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542227-why-patricia-of-bollingbroke-sucks#post1542227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, one of the - and against my preferred view - if not the first big Anarch, who is built in text as the greatest agitator and rebel of the Anarchs and Brujah, also lacks any weight to her doings and will. Putting it plainly she sucks, and I wished it weren't so.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the fact that she was the wife of a killed peasant who took a famous peasant leader as a lover, all of whom seem to be way more important than herself in her own story. And that trend continue... Robin freaking Hood Embraces her and takes her out of jail. And she takes the name of her late lover, so she buries her own identity even further in lieu of other guys.<br /> <br /> Than she kills the crap baron who made her miserable, which is very cool. But instead of staying in England, and fighting... I don't know... a thousand year old tyrant like Mithras, or Queen Anne, she runs away. And goes to... Spain, where she... basically stumbles on Anarchs... who basically stumble on Hardestadt's castle? which sometimes is in Bavaria and sometimes in Spain? and then a band of untrained, kind of lost fledlings, murder one of the most powerful Ventrue of the current time, in his own castle... Someone Patricia could've never had heard of before.<br /> And ... in the end, Hardestadt is not dead! So she probably looked like a chump?! I don't know. This 'Hardestadt is not dead' spiel always was weird for me, did they call the Anarchs out? What happened? Either way... Anarch War goes, nothing important occurs for Patricia, maybe just some agitating or not<br /> <br /> Then Convention of Thorns! Our Rebel Leader, who is determined to kill Hardestadt now, for some reason. Tries to kill him, and fails because guns are nothing to vampires.... she didn't tried before? She think someone with Fortitude wouldn't take those shot? And let me remind you that of all the elders she could attack, like the ones in her homeland, she decided to attack the guy she just kind of stumbled into killing, and &quot;failed&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> And... we skip a lot of time, she changes her name; she runs, Helena comes into contact with Patricia, and bam, methuseleah puppet of Helena forever.... than they go to America (because why would two centuries-old elders go anywhere else) and bicker with Critias, because Helena. And then she starts to like... planes? funny, but I can understand it perfectly, just a bit random.<br /> So she jobs for Helena, then runs again to NY, and starts jobbing for Lambach Ruthven... and that's that... Great leader she is, great symbol; not even a tragic story, it just feels accidentally pathetic I don't know.<br /> <br /> Any information I'm missing that throws new light into her?<br /> <br /> Are my views a bit true?<br /> <br /> Is there a way to make her stand with dignity alongside Gratiano, Vykos, Dominique de Tourraine, Vasantasena, Lugoj?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic post.<br /> <br /> Patricia Bollingbrook AKA Tyler is one of my favorite characters in V:TM and I'm very glad that she managed to make a return to prominence in 5th Edition proper even if it is as a &quot;legend&quot; the Anarchs have decided to trot out again. I feel like so many of the Chicago by Night characters got dropped like hot potatoes after CBN Second Edition and never got mentioned after that book even when they would have had major importance to things like the Anarch Movement. Transylvania Chronicles averted this with Tyler.<br /> <br /> I do think your description lacks a bit of nuance, though, that deserves to have a few points brought up.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Being a sellout is Tyler's thing</b>: One of the early things in the depiction of the Brujah was that they were supposed to follow a trajectory of starting as Anarchs then moving to compromisers then becoming indistinguishable from other Elders. Basically, the Winston Churchill quote about anyone who isn't a liberal while young has no heart and isn't conservative when they're old has no brain. She's an illustration of someone who was a firebrand rebel that saw her revolution fail and decided to get smart by becoming a Camarilla Elder. Even so, she helps the Anarchs behind the scenes while using them for her own ends. Probably telling herself she's playing the long game (while actually being Helena's puppet).<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Sabbat are worse than the Camarilla</b>: This is a matter of opinion but one that I believe Transylvania Chronicles was trying to forward. Because the Kindred who refuse to buckle down and accept the Camarilla's peace respond by...massacring an entire village of men, women, and children unrelated to the Convention of Thorns. This was my reaction when my Tremere (pretending to be Tzimisce) character on Humanity saw the aftermath of starting the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"600\" height=\"500\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/C5612AQE3S0QdnFvxUw/article-cover_image-shrink_600_2000/0/1532018235487?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=-iCZEARmFSx3Jmaa5cTWko0vSePXOSTAjk1daadudIE\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/C5612AQE3S0QdnFvxUw/article-cover_image-shrink_600_2000/0/1532018235487?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=-iCZEARmFSx3Jmaa5cTWko0vSePXOSTAjk1daadudIE\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/C5612AQE3S0QdnFvxUw/article-cover_image-shrink_600_2000/0/1532018235487?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=-iCZEARmFSx3Jmaa5cTWko0vSePXOSTAjk1daadudIE\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> 3. <b>Tyler isn't in charge of her own opinion anyway</b>: As stated, she goes where Helena says for her to do and just rationalizes it the way she wants to later. This is EVERY vampire and railroady plots like TC actually are probably how they have to live. Gratiano, Lujo, and others are all dancing to the Antediluvians tunes anyway. Indeed, it's how I justify why Lucita chose to do a 180 and become Moncada.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T15:44:52-07:00","id":1542339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542227-why-patricia-of-bollingbroke-sucks?p=1542331#post1542331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, there's no ability to do a rebellion in England against Mithras.<br /> <br /> <b>WHY THERE ARE NO ANARCHS IN ENGLAND</b><br /> <br /> This actually came up in my FALL OF LONDON campaign where one of the players explained that the Anarchs are a new phenomenon and only came into existence after WW2.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Mithras never had to deal with any internal rebellion. There was no Anarch revolt in England.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Bullshit, every Prince does.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Every Camarilla Prince but Mithras was not a prince. He was a god.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All the more reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;*deliberate sigh* Listen, dipshit, I'm not speaking figuratively. I'm saying that when you met Mithras, you believed he was a god and wanted to worship him. He was the fairest, bestest, most awesome son of a bitch who ever lived. His power over making you love him was beyond question and the only people who could challenge that were other ancients that were just as powerful. Mithras hated the Tremere because the Council of Seven could do that. Maybe the Inner Council. Some Red Listers. Plus, Mithras thought he was a benevolent tyrant and tried to act that way.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Bullshit. No such thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, but the Anarchs are still vampires and they can only propose something similar. Richard II, for example, was the first King of England to ever have his head on a block. That was because Mithras hated him for breaking his word to the rebels. Hence why Henry the Fourth came to power a few decades later.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's a fucking fairy tale if I ever heard it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And yet it's the story people believed. Because Mithras wanted them to. So they did.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras has also been in Torpor for massive amounts of time over the years. Its one of the story plot points with his child Cret from Lair of the hidden. He gets bored of whatever Empire is current and takes a nice long nap, and waits for whoever he put in charge to wake him up when things get interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T22:30:41-07:00","id":1542352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542227-why-patricia-of-bollingbroke-sucks?p=1542332#post1542332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fantastic post.<br /> <br /> Patricia Bollingbrook AKA Tyler is one of my favorite characters in V:TM and I'm very glad that she managed to make a return to prominence in 5th Edition proper even if it is as a &quot;legend&quot; the Anarchs have decided to trot out again. I feel like so many of the Chicago by Night characters got dropped like hot potatoes after CBN Second Edition and never got mentioned after that book even when they would have had major importance to things like the Anarch Movement. Transylvania Chronicles averted this with Tyler.<br /> <br /> I do think your description lacks a bit of nuance, though, that deserves to have a few points brought up.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Being a sellout is Tyler's thing</b>: One of the early things in the depiction of the Brujah was that they were supposed to follow a trajectory of starting as Anarchs then moving to compromisers then becoming indistinguishable from other Elders. Basically, the Winston Churchill quote about anyone who isn't a liberal while young has no heart and isn't conservative when they're old has no brain. She's an illustration of someone who was a firebrand rebel that saw her revolution fail and decided to get smart by becoming a Camarilla Elder. Even so, she helps the Anarchs behind the scenes while using them for her own ends. Probably telling herself she's playing the long game (while actually being Helena's puppet).<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Sabbat are worse than the Camarilla</b>: This is a matter of opinion but one that I believe Transylvania Chronicles was trying to forward. Because the Kindred who refuse to buckle down and accept the Camarilla's peace respond by...massacring an entire village of men, women, and children unrelated to the Convention of Thorns. This was my reaction when my Tremere (pretending to be Tzimisce) character on Humanity saw the aftermath of starting the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"600\" height=\"500\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/C5612AQE3S0QdnFvxUw/article-cover_image-shrink_600_2000/0/1532018235487?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=-iCZEARmFSx3Jmaa5cTWko0vSePXOSTAjk1daadudIE\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/C5612AQE3S0QdnFvxUw/article-cover_image-shrink_600_2000/0/1532018235487?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=-iCZEARmFSx3Jmaa5cTWko0vSePXOSTAjk1daadudIE\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/C5612AQE3S0QdnFvxUw/article-cover_image-shrink_600_2000/0/1532018235487?e=2147483647&amp;v=beta&amp;t=-iCZEARmFSx3Jmaa5cTWko0vSePXOSTAjk1daadudIE\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> 3. <b>Tyler isn't in charge of her own opinion anyway</b>: As stated, she goes where Helena says for her to do and just rationalizes it the way she wants to later. This is EVERY vampire and railroady plots like TC actually are probably how they have to live. Gratiano, Lujo, and others are all dancing to the Antediluvians tunes anyway. Indeed, it's how I justify why Lucita chose to do a 180 and become Moncada.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the contribution. I can see it. Although I still think even only reading from Children of the Inquisition, or reading all her material, I feel like this &quot;arc&quot; of Brujah getting Ventrued was almost accidental, and not quite planned. I could be wrong of course! But I don't feel intention behind it. Maybe after Thorns she might've been kind of down and fizzled out, but the use of her character in the setting I felt that didn't reach a good Persona or Story. Not a story of failed rebellion, nor of a rebel tiring itself, nor one of a rebel turned tyrant... Not intentionally either way.<br /> <br /> In my view, she is presented as OG ANARCH ICON. And does not reach such a height, not even in-universe as a story to be told between Anarchs. But we CAN salvage it as such a story of icon, failing, turning into the enemy, or something like that. Since we lack so much true heroes (even if as mundane and down to earth as a rebel wanting to kill tyrants) I do want to play her straight as an Icon (not a clean, pure paladinite one, cuz that is idealistic even for a game, specially for Vampire).<br /> <br /> All that is just my view and a bit of frustration. Don't want to undermine no one's interpretation, nor even necessarily all her writers. But the thread is helping me get somewhere!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T23:58:21-07:00","id":1542354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542227-why-patricia-of-bollingbroke-sucks?p=1542352#post1542352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the contribution. I can see it. Although I still think even only reading from Children of the Inquisition, or reading all her material, I feel like this &quot;arc&quot; of Brujah getting Ventrued was almost accidental, and not quite planned. I could be wrong of course! But I don't feel intention behind it. Maybe after Thorns she might've been kind of down and fizzled out, but the use of her character in the setting I felt that didn't reach a good Persona or Story. Not a story of failed rebellion, nor of a rebel tiring itself, nor one of a rebel turned tyrant... Not intentionally either way.<br /> <br /> In my view, she is presented as OG ANARCH ICON. And does not reach such a height, not even in-universe as a story to be told between Anarchs. But we CAN salvage it as such a story of icon, failing, turning into the enemy, or something like that. Since we lack so much true heroes (even if as mundane and down to earth as a rebel wanting to kill tyrants) I do want to play her straight as an Icon (not a clean, pure paladinite one, cuz that is idealistic even for a game, specially for Vampire).<br /> <br /> All that is just my view and a bit of frustration. Don't want to undermine no one's interpretation, nor even necessarily all her writers. But the thread is helping me get somewhere!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring her up as the OG Brujah sellout was because that was a running theme in CBN. Juggler is the first Anarch we meet and he's an ineffectual wannabe Anarch leader who answers directly to Tyler. It's all but stated that the Anarchs in Chicago are useless after Maldavis because Juggler is there to keep them useless but occupied with pointless acts of defiance. Sort of like how J Edgar Hoover actually employed a lot of communist leaders with bribes to know who was in the actual movement (to the point that a lot of them were paid for by him).<br /> <br /> We know that she betrayed Maldavis for power in the Council Wars too and she was set up as a genuine Anarch social reformer.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat wanted to also blackmail her into helping them by knowing her real name/identity so the one in Chicago is actually in hiding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}